From 0ab740a6afad489a5b63a6046de00f2406015616 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexei Starovoitov <ast@kernel.org>
Date: Wed, 13 May 2020 16:03:53 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] bpf: backport CAP_BPF with separate monitoring
 permissions

Backport capability 39 and the permission split to this tree's BPF
program types, privileged map types, BTF, ID lookup and loader checks.
Network programs require BPF plus NET_ADMIN; tracing requires BPF plus
PERFMON. Preserve SYS_ADMIN as the compatibility fallback for BPF and PERFMON.

Keep pointer-disclosing verifier and array-map privileges behind PERFMON.
The legacy raw instruction dumper does not sanitize kernel addresses, so
require monitoring privilege in addition to BPF for raw dumps. Restrict
probe_write_user to SYS_ADMIN as upstream does. A denied trace_printk
helper must return NULL instead of falling through to get_socket_cookie.

Adapted from Linux commits:
commit a17b53c4a4b5 ("bpf, capability: Introduce CAP_BPF")
commit 2c78ee898d8f ("bpf: Implement CAP_BPF")

Features absent from this tree, such as bounded loops and bpf-to-bpf
calls, are not advertised or introduced by this permission backport.

Backport notes: combine capability definition and permission split; adapt
to existing program types and verifier. Adapted by ivanmeler.

Signed-off-by: ivanmeler <i_ivan@windowslive.com>
